{"t": 784.933, "n": 223, "ev": "result", "ok": true, "text": "The code step is not finished: the preview hasn't returned a result, and the gate may time out again. I changed no file this visit, so the tree is the same one the gate last ran.\n\nThe engine and package work of every plan row is done, and the plan is `completed` with all rows marked. The report `docs/tasks/i203a.report.md` is already written.\n\n**What I measured**\n- The package suite alone, `cd plugins/temperspec-tgraph && python -m pytest -q tests`, gave **717 passed in 682 s**, exit 0.\n- The engine suite takes about 25–30 minutes on this machine. It also runs the package's own tests, through the engine's `test_workflow_packages.py`.\n- The code gate's check has a single 1800 s limit (`check_timeout_s=1800` in `workflow/temperspec/__init__.py:275`) for all four commands together.\n- The previous gate's exit -9 on the package suite is therefore a time-limit kill, not a test failure. The engine suite, `ruff` and `mypy` had already run at the gate; the package suite got what was left of the 1800 s and was cut off at about 40%.\n\n**What I did**\n- I started `tempergraph self-check bbb98b6286f68261eebb72c277e56908` once on the unchanged tree.\n- It was still running with empty output when I stopped waiting.\n- The gate reuses a command's recorded result for an unchanged tree. If the preview finishes, the gate should run nothing new. If it doesn't, the gate will have the same time pressure as last time.\n\nI can't confirm `tests_passed: yes`, because no preview has returned a pass.\n\n**Decision for you:** the check limit is not enough for these four commands on this machine. Either raise `check_timeout_s` on the code gate, or run the verification on faster hardware. I did not change either, because that is outside the plan's rows and would change the tree.\n\nThe `stamp.json`, `authoring.json` and `diagram/` refresh is still for the operator, as the report says.\n\nARTIFACT code_report: docs/tasks/i203a.report.md\nARTIFACT tests_passed: no", "subtype": "success", "is_error": false, "session_id": "2673cfb0-0658-48c8-b55a-2d07a19a7793"}
